🚀 Steps to Set Up Your RSSBDMS Frontend Demo
1. Initialize a New Frontend Project
Use a modern frontend framework like React with Next.js for optimal performance and scalability.
Create a new Next.js app:
bash
CopyEdit
  npx create-next-app@latest rssbdms-frontend
  cd rssbdms-frontend
Install necessary dependencies:
bash
CopyEdit
  npm install
2. Implement Mock Data
Create a data directory to store your mock JSON files representing members, contributions, and benefits.
Example: data/members.json
json
CopyEdit
  [
    {
      "member_id": "001",
      "name": "John Doe",
      "date_of_birth": "1990-01-01",
      "gender": "Male",
      "contact_info": {
        "email": "john.doe@example.com",
        "phone": "+250788123456"
      },
      "address": "Kigali, Rwanda",
      "registration_date": "2025-01-15"
    }
    // Add more member objects
  ]
Repeat similar structures for contributions.json and benefits.json.
3. Design the User Interface
Login Page: Create a login form that authenticates users using the provided credentials.
Dashboard:
oTop Bar: Include branding elements like the RSSB logo, system name, and tagline.
oSidebar Navigation: Provide links to modules such as Member Registration, Contributions Tracking, and Benefit Processing.
oMain Content Area: Display data fetched from the mock JSON files.
4. Implement Multilingual Support
Use a library like react-i18next to add multilingual capabilities.
Installation:
bash
CopyEdit
  npm install react-i18next i18next
Configuration: Set up translation files for Kinyarwanda, French, and English.
5. Deploy to Vercel
Initialize a Git Repository:
bash
CopyEdit
  git init
  git add .
  git commit -m "Initial commit"
Push to GitHub:
bash
CopyEdit
  git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/rssbdms-frontend.git
  git push -u origin main
Deploy on Vercel:
oSign in to Vercel and import your GitHub repository.
oFollow the prompts to deploy your project.
oOnce deployed, Vercel will provide a live URL (e.g., https://rssbdms-frontend.vercel.app) for testing.

